# .dockerignore sits next to the build context root and filters what
# `docker build` sends to the daemon. It is the .gitignore of Docker builds.

# --- node_modules: the #1 mistake ---
# If this is missing, your HOST node_modules (macOS binaries, wrong platform,
# gigabytes of junk) gets sent as build context and a stray COPY can bake it
# into the image. Dependencies are installed INSIDE the image, never copied.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- build artifacts: rebuilt inside the image ---
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist

# --- secrets and environment ---
# NEVER ship these: `COPY . .` would bake them into a layer permanently,
# even if you delete the file in a later instruction (it stays in layer
# history). Runtime config goes in via -e / orchestrator env / secret manager.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
*.pem
*.key

# --- version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# --- editor/OS noise (also just slows the build context upload) ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log

# --- docker files themselves ---
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore

# --- docs and tests not needed inside the image ---
README.md
LEARNING.md
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
